[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Feather has been installed to %%FEATHER_DIR%%.

Configuration lives in %%ETCDIR%%. Two starting points were installed as
samples; copy and edit them before starting the service:

  cp %%ETCDIR%%/server.exs.sample   %%ETCDIR%%/server.exs
  cp %%ETCDIR%%/pipeline.exs.sample %%ETCDIR%%/pipeline.exs

Further worked examples (MSA, spam filtering, rate limiting, tarpitting)
are in %%EXAMPLESDIR%%.

Then enable and start it:

  sysrc feather_enable=YES
  service feather start

Logs are written to %%FEATHER_LOGDIR%%.

A dedicated %%FEATHER_USER%%:%%FEATHER_GROUP%% account owns the config, log
and run directories.

The service itself still starts as root, because it binds the privileged
SMTP ports (25, 465 and 587) and does not drop privileges on its own. If you
have arranged unprivileged access to those ports (mac_portacl, a redirector,
or net.inet.ip.portrange.reservedhigh), set:

  sysrc feather_user=%%FEATHER_USER%%
EOM
}
]
